<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kanazawa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kanazawa is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-japan">Sea of Japan</a> coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honshu">Honshu</a> and the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ishikawa-prefecture">Ishikawa Prefecture</a>. It grew from a temple centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ikko-ikki">Ikko-ikki</a> founded in 1546 into the castle town of the Maeda lords of Kaga, one of the largest cities of Edo-period <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. Spared bombing in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, it keeps old districts, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kenroku-en">Kenroku-en</a> garden and crafts such as gold leaf.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kanazawa.jpg" alt="Kanazawa" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 金沢市 · CC BY 2.1 jp · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%9C%9B%E6%B9%96%E5%8F%B0%EF%BC%92.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
